# An independent conformance target with distinct failure outcomes

## Goal

Run the `wotex_conformance` runner against the core package as an external
subject: the Lab target is a separate operating-system process started
through a port with explicit code paths, it receives one request on standard
input and answers one observation, and it never sees an expectation. Both
bundled corpora pass, a changed archive is refused before any vector runs,
and unsupported operations and malformed documents produce distinct outcomes
rather than a pass.

## Prerequisites

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:wotex_lab, "~> 0.1.0"},
  {:wotex_conformance, "~> 0.1.0"}
])
```

The requirements above are published-artifact requirements. At the time this
notebook was written none of the `wotex*` packages is published on Hex; the
notebook is verified against the workspace source cohort recorded in
`docs/provenance/source-cohort.json` by `test/wotex/lab/cookbook_test.exs`,
which evaluates every Elixir cell below in order (skipping this install
cell). `Mix.install/1` never points at a Git checkout. The subject archive
is a tar of the loaded core `ebin` directory written under a temporary
directory named here and removed at the end; this is source-mode evidence,
not a Hex artifact claim.

## Package and consumer ownership

| Concern | Owner | Where |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Claims, vectors, expectations, statuses, report | `wotex_conformance` (package-implements) | `Wotex.Conformance.Corpus`, `Runner`, `Report` |
| The subject under test | `wotex` | `Wotex.ThingDescription`, `Wotex.ThingModel` |
| The external target process and its derivation | `wotex_lab` (consumer) | `Wotex.Lab.Conformance.Target` |
| Process containment (paths, `HOME`, timeout, output bound) | this notebook as host | the `External` definition below |

## Run

```elixir
alias Wotex.Conformance.{Corpus, Report, Runner, Subject}
alias Wotex.Conformance.Target.External
alias Wotex.Lab.Conformance.Target
alias Wotex.Lab.Telemetry

telemetry_id = "cookbook-conformance-#{System.unique_integer([:positive])}"

events =
  for component <- Telemetry.components(),
      operation <- Telemetry.operations(),
      event <- [:start, :stop, :exception],
      do: [:wotex, :lab, component, operation, event]

:ok = :telemetry.attach_many(telemetry_id, events, &Telemetry.forward/4, self())
generated_at = ~U[2026-09-07 12:00:00Z]
```

The subject archive names the compiled core that will answer; its digest is
part of the subject identity the runner checks.

```elixir
tmp_dir = Path.join(System.tmp_dir!(), "wotex-lab-cookbook-conformance-#{System.unique_integer([:positive])}")
File.mkdir_p!(tmp_dir)
archive = Path.join(tmp_dir, "core-ebin.tar")

:ok =
  :erl_tar.create(
    String.to_charlist(archive),
    [{~c"ebin", String.to_charlist(Application.app_dir(:wotex, "ebin"))}],
    [:compressed]
  )

digest = "sha256:" <> Base.encode16(:crypto.hash(:sha256, File.read!(archive)), case: :lower)

{:ok, subject} =
  Subject.from_map(%{
    "id" => "wotex.core",
    "version" => to_string(Application.spec(:wotex, :vsn)),
    "artifact_digest" => digest,
    "interface" => %{"kind" => "lab_target", "revision" => "1"}
  })

{subject.id, subject.version}
```

The external target: `erl` with explicit code paths, no shell, a private
`HOME`, a wall-clock timeout and an output ceiling. The runner substitutes
the subject archive path; nothing else reaches the target.

```elixir
erl = Path.join([to_string(:code.root_dir()), "bin", "erl"])

code_paths =
  Enum.flat_map([:elixir, :wotex, :jason, :ex_json_schema, :wotex_lab, :wotex_runtime, :nx, :telemetry], fn app ->
    ["-pa", to_string(:code.lib_dir(app, :ebin))]
  end)

eval =
  "application:ensure_all_started(elixir), " <>
    "'Elixir.Wotex.Lab.Conformance.Target':main([unicode:characters_to_binary(A) || A <- init:get_plain_arguments()])"

target = fn ->
  {:ok, target} =
    External.from_map(%{
      executable: erl,
      args: ["-noshell"] ++ code_paths ++ ["-eval", eval, "-extra", "--archive", "{subject_archive}"],
      artifact_path: archive,
      environment: %{"HOME" => tmp_dir},
      timeout_ms: 30_000,
      max_output_bytes: 1_048_576
    })

  target
end

Path.basename(erl)
```

Both bundled corpora, each vector answered by a fresh target process.

```elixir
run_corpus = fn name ->
  {:ok, corpus} = Corpus.load(Application.app_dir(:wotex_conformance, "priv/vectors/" <> name))

  {:ok, %Report{} = report} =
    Runner.run(corpus, subject, target.(), generated_at: generated_at, environment: %{"runtime" => "wotex_lab"})

  {:ok, encoded} = Report.encode(report)
  failures = report.results |> Enum.reject(&(&1.status == :pass)) |> Enum.map(&{&1.vector_id, &1.status})
  %{vectors: length(corpus.vectors), summary: report.summary, failures: failures, encoded: encoded}
end

td_report = run_corpus.("thing-description-1.1")
tm_report = run_corpus.("thing-model-1.1")
{td_report.summary, tm_report.summary, td_report.failures, tm_report.failures}
```

## Deliberate breakage

A subject whose archive digest does not match is refused before any vector
runs: every result is an infrastructure error, none a pass or a fail. The
target's derivation, called in-process, reports unsupported operations and
non-object documents as their own outcomes.

```elixir
{:ok, forged} =
  Subject.from_map(%{
    "id" => "wotex.core",
    "version" => "0.0.0",
    "artifact_digest" => "sha256:" <> String.duplicate("0", 64),
    "interface" => %{"kind" => "lab_target", "revision" => "1"}
  })

{:ok, tm_corpus} = Corpus.load(Application.app_dir(:wotex_conformance, "priv/vectors/thing-model-1.1"))
{:ok, refused} = Runner.run(tm_corpus, forged, target.(), generated_at: generated_at, environment: %{})

request = fn operation, input ->
  %{"claim" => %{"operation" => operation}, "vector" => %{"id" => "v", "input" => input}}
end

document = %{
  "@context" => Wotex.td_context_1_1(),
  "title" => "Lamp",
  "security" => ["nosec_sc"],
  "securityDefinitions" => %{"nosec_sc" => %{"scheme" => "nosec"}}
}

observed = Target.respond(request.("thing_description.parse", %{"document" => document, "projection" => ["/title"]}))
unsupported = Target.respond(request.("discovery.list", %{}))
non_object = Target.respond(request.("thing_model.parse", %{"document" => "not-an-object"}))
{:error, missing_archive} = Target.run([], fn -> "{}" end)
{:error, undecodable} = Target.run(["--archive", archive], fn -> "{" end)

{refused.summary, observed["actual"], unsupported["outcome"], non_object["actual"]["errors"], missing_archive, undecodable}
```

```elixir
{:ok, _removed} = File.rm_rf(tmp_dir)
```

## Safe telemetry

The in-process derivation emits a conformance span whose only labels are the
operation name and the outcome; documents and vector inputs are absent.

```elixir
drain = fn drain ->
  receive do
    {:wotex_lab_telemetry, event, measurements, metadata} ->
      [{event, measurements, metadata} | drain.(drain)]
  after
    0 -> []
  end
end

spans = drain.(drain)
:telemetry.detach(telemetry_id)

operations =
  for {[:wotex, :lab, :conformance, :conformance, :stop], _measurements, metadata} <- spans,
      do: metadata.operation

text = inspect(spans)
labels_safe? = operations != [] and not (text =~ "Lamp") and not (text =~ "not-an-object")
{Enum.uniq(operations), labels_safe?}
```

## Expected output

| Check | Expectation |
| --- | --- |
| `td-corpus-pass` | Every Thing Description vector passes (14 of 14) |
| `tm-corpus-pass` | Every Thing Model vector passes (6 of 6) |
| `changed-archive-refused` | A forged digest yields `infrastructure_error` for every vector |
| `unsupported-operation` | `discovery.list` is `unsupported` with `operation_not_implemented` |
| `non-object-refused` | A string document is `object_required`; a missing archive is exit 11; undecodable input is exit 14 |
| `no-expectations-in-target` | The reports never carry the vector documents, and the target request carries no expectation |

```elixir
%{
  "td-corpus-pass" => td_report.failures == [] and td_report.summary["pass"] == 14 and td_report.vectors == 14,
  "tm-corpus-pass" => tm_report.failures == [] and tm_report.summary["pass"] == 6 and tm_report.vectors == 6,
  "changed-archive-refused" => refused.summary["infrastructure_error"] == length(tm_corpus.vectors),
  "unsupported-operation" =>
    unsupported["outcome"] == "unsupported" and unsupported["codes"] == ["operation_not_implemented"] and
      observed["actual"] == %{"accepted" => true, "document" => %{"/title" => "Lamp"}},
  "non-object-refused" =>
    match?([%{"code" => "object_required"}], non_object["actual"]["errors"]) and missing_archive == 11 and
      undecodable == 14,
  "no-expectations-in-target" =>
    not (td_report.encoded =~ "Minimal Thing") and not Map.has_key?(request.("x", %{}), "expectation") and
      labels_safe?
}
```

## Public seam

`lab.conformance_target` is Lab-owned: the runner's external protocol is
package documentation, the Lab target implements it against the core
package, and the runner project never imports the subject.

## Spec and completion IDs

* Lab: WLB.06 (`WLB-C07`, `WLB-C08`).
* Upstream consumer evidence: `WCF-C01`, `WCF-C02`, `WCF-C03`, `WCF-C04`.
  `WCF-C05` (Discovery corpus) is an explicit excluded corpus decision, not a
  pass.

## Replacement adapter

A target for another implementation is a separate executable that reads one
JSON request line, answers one JSON response line with the same `protocol`
and `outcome` vocabulary, and exits with the documented codes. Wrap it in
`Wotex.Conformance.Target.External` with your own code paths, environment,
timeout and output bound; the runner, corpora and expectations do not change.
